#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:5 c53ec79445a24686a885b6f5cde2fc92
msgid "Manual tuning of Roll and Pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:7 f6a1d842117b45898a155065c0031fb3
msgid ""
"Manual tuning may be required to provide a stable tune before Autotune is"
" run, or if Autotune does not produce an acceptable tune. The process "
"below can be done on roll and pitch at the same time for a quick manual "
"tune **provided the aircraft is symmetrical**. If the aircraft is not "
"symmetrical, then the process should be done for roll and pitch "
"individually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:9 9af3251e7adf405082f6e2da6def9d54
msgid ""
"The pilot should be especially careful to ensure that "
":ref:`ATC_THR_MIX_MAN <ATC_THR_MIX_MAN>` and :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER "
"<MOT_THST_HOVER>` are set correctly before manual tuning is started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:11 0f5255d08f8e42fe8b7e087b984839ac
msgid ""
"When oscillations start do not make large or sudden stick inputs. Reduce "
"the throttle smoothly to land the aircraft while using very slow and "
"small roll and pitch inputs to control the aircraft position. For each "
"axis:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:14 e196f6b00190477c9e8ba0a6e6556458
#, python-format
msgid ""
"If the vehicle already oscillates in an axis, first lower the P, D, and I"
" terms in 50% steps until stable, before starting manual tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:16 8100c02ebc1747828223b1053eee5877
#, python-format
msgid "Increase the D term in steps of 50% until oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:17 89ea15a54f7d4d1e83cbd73ccce9b4df
#, python-format
msgid "Reduce the D term in steps of 10% until the oscillation disappears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:18 0aeef82304ae470e94868eb9ffe4f2dc
msgid "Reduce the D term by a further 25%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:19 0dcc2d38daea4cf4b26fd9be3ddddf71
#, python-format
msgid "Increase the P term in steps of 50% until oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:20 7c162319f5e54b13b85c7b0d457bd695
#, python-format
msgid "Reduce the P term in steps of 10% until the oscillation disappears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:21 b6ba755bd50e44b188d3ae0bde780580
msgid "Reduce the P term by a further 25%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:23 7c0f7f824f5d4cf99bb7cbc546bbade2
msgid ""
"Each time the P term is changed set the I term equal to the P term. Those"
" parameters can be changed on ground and preferably disarmed. A confident"
" pilot could set them in flight with GCS or transmitter tuning knob (see "
":ref:`Transmitter based tuning<common-transmitter-tuning>` page for setup"
" of this feature)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac_rollpitchtuning.rst:27 6280602a979a42538760d910e9ceeea7
msgid ""
"If using :ref:`Transmitter based tuning<common-transmitter-tuning>`, set "
"the minimum value of the tuning range to the current safe value and the "
"upper range to approximately 4 times the current value. Be careful not to"
" move the slider before the parameter list is refreshed to recover the "
"set value. Ensure the transmitter tuning is switched off before setting "
"the parameter value or the tuning may immediately overwrite it."
msgstr ""

